{
    "background_story": "Eugene was a reclusive novelist who lived in a secluded cabin on the outskirts of town. He spent most of his days writing and researching, rarely venturing out into the world. But one fateful night, a fierce storm befell the region, knocking out the power and isolating Eugene from the outside world. As the tempest raged on, a massive tree branch crashed through the cabin's roof, destroying his life's work and leaving him injured. As Eugene struggled to come to terms with the loss, he realized that the disaster had also brought him a strange sense of liberation. He began to write again, this time with a newfound sense of purpose and creativity. The storm that had befallen him had also brought him a chance to start anew, and Eugene's writing career was reborn from the ashes of his old life.",
